  depression, distress\\n23. OQ-45.2 feedback Norway: Feedback using Norwegian version of OQ-Analyst with Outcome       
  Questionnaire-45.2 (PROM) vs no feedback; measures quality of services\\n24. DSCAN cancer app: Facilitates symptom    
  reporting (via ESAS PROM) and provides information/recommendations vs control; measures quality of life and           
  activation\\n29. PRIME-MD psychiatric screening: Telling patient and/or physician PRIME-MD results (computerized      
  psychiatric screening PROM) vs neither told; measures psychiatric consultation/referral\\n30. Diabetes Telephone      
  Study: Automated interactive voice response tool providing real-time patient-reported data (symptoms/side effects)    
  to physicians vs non-interactive educational calls; measures patient-reported outcomes\\n32. Cancer psychosocial      
  interventions: Making patient-reported cancer needs, QOL, and psychosocial information available to healthcare team   
  for coordinated interventions vs not seen; measures QOL and psychosocial functioning\\n33. ZELF-i depression trial:   
  Systematic self-monitoring (tracking depressive symptoms as PROMs) plus weekly personalized feedback vs no            
  additional intervention; measures depressive symptoms and psychosocial functioning\\n\\nEXCLUDED STUDIES (14):\\n4.   
  MeMOS trial: Both groups receive feedback (therapist+supervisor vs therapist-only); lacks true no-feedback            
  control\\n6. Graphical PRO displays: Literature review, not a randomised trial\\n9. Depression screening in family    
  practice: One-time depression screening feedback to physicians, not ongoing PROMs feedback\\n10. DUI offender study:  
  Laboratory study on alcohol impairment feedback, not PROMs feedback in healthcare\\n12. SF-36 validation: Validation  
  study of questionnaire properties, not RCT comparing PROMs feedback to no feedback\\n16. Metastatic prostate cancer   
  intervention: Insufficient information to confirm PROMs feedback component\\n17. PROMs impact review: Structured      
  review, not a randomised trial\\n18. VTE risk study: Observational study using linked records, not an RCT\\n20.       
  Self-care tool validation: Tool development/validation study, not RCT comparing PROMs feedback to no feedback\\n25.   
  PRO graphic formats evaluation: Cross-sectional study evaluating PRO formats, not RCT comparing feedback to no        
  feedback\\n26. Preoperative knowledge feedback: Intervention is knowledge-test feedback (not PROMs feedback)\\n27.    
  Depression severity interviews: Qualitative interview study, not a randomised trial\\n28. Stroke self-management      
  feasibility: Unclear if involves PROMs feedback to healthcare professionals or patients\\n31. HRQL assessment in      
  oncology: Compares HRQL assessment with/without interpretation, not feedback vs no feedback\",\n                      
  \"additional_context\": \"Screening conducted according to Cochrane Handbook guidelines: conservative approach (when  
  in doubt, include), individual rationale for each study, consideration of population, intervention, comparison,       
